      "source": [
        "# 33. Authority Framing\n",
        "\n",
        "[![Open In Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg)](https://colab.research.google.com/github/amerob/ultimate-prompt-engineering-playbook/blob/main/notebooks/04-role-playing/33_authority_framing.ipynb)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Category**: Role-Playing & Persona\n",
        "\n",
        "**Technique #33** | Difficulty: Intermediate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Description\n",
        "\n",
        "Authority Framing leverages the psychological principle that people tend to trust and follow authority figures. By framing the AI as an authority or having it cite authoritative sources and frameworks, responses gain credibility, confidence, and persuasive power. This technique is particularly effective for advice, recommendations, and persuasive content.\n",
        "\n",
        "### When to Use:\n",
        "- Need to build credibility and trust\n",
        "- Providing recommendations or advice\n",
        "- Creating persuasive content\n",
        "- Establishing expertise in a response\n",
        "- Supporting arguments with authority\n",
        "\n",
        "### Key Benefits:\n",
        "✓ Increases perceived credibility of responses\n",
        "✓ Builds user trust and confidence\n",
        "✓ Strengthens persuasive arguments\n",
        "✓ Provides framework-based reasoning\n",
        "✓ Reduces skepticism in recommendations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## How It Works\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
        "│                  AUTHORITY FRAMING MODEL                    │\n",
        "└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
        "\n",
        "    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
        "    │              AUTHORITY SIGNALS                      │\n",
        "    ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n",
        "    │  • Credentials: Degrees, certifications, experience │\n",
        "    │  • Institutions: Universities, companies, orgs    │\n",
        "    │  • Frameworks: Established methodologies            │\n",
        "    │  • Data: Statistics, research, case studies         │\n",
        "    │  • Recognition: Awards, publications, testimonials  │\n",
        "    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
        "                              │\n",
        "                              ▼\n",
        "    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
        "    │              CREDIBILITY BUILDING                   │\n",
        "    ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n",
        "    │  ✓ Reference authoritative sources                  │\n",
        "    │  ✓ Use established frameworks                       │\n",
        "    │  ✓ Cite research and data                           │\n",
        "    │  ✓ Demonstrate expertise                            │\n",
        "    │  ✓ Show track record of success                     │\n",
        "    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
        "                              │\n",
        "                              ▼\n",
        "    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
        "    │              AUTHORITATIVE OUTPUT                   │\n",
        "    ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n",
        "    │  ✓ Confident, evidence-based responses              │\n",
        "    │  ✓ Framework-grounded recommendations               │\n",
        "    │  ✓ Data-supported conclusions                       │\n",
        "    │  ✓ Expert-level insights                            │\n",
        "    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "### Authority Types:\n",
        "1. **Positional**: Based on role or title\n",
        "2. **Expert**: Based on knowledge and credentials\n",
        "3. **Referent**: Based on trust and relationships\n",
        "4. **Coercive**: Based on ability to enforce (use carefully)\n",
        "5. **Informational**: Based on data and evidence"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Setup\n",
        "\n",
        "Install required packages and configure API access."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Install required packages\n",
        "!pip install openai -q\n",
        "\n",
        "# Import libraries\n",
        "import os\n",
        "from getpass import getpass\n",
        "from openai import OpenAI\n",
        "\n",
        "# Setup API key (secure input)\n",
        "api_key = getpass(\"Enter your OpenAI API key: \")\n",
        "client = OpenAI(api_key=api_key)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"✓ Setup complete!\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Basic Example\n",
        "\n",
        "Comparing responses with and without authority framing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def get_authority_response(prompt, authority_frame=None, model=\"gpt-4o-mini\"):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Get response with optional authority framing.\n",
        "    \n",
        "    Args:\n",
        "        prompt: User's question or request\n",
        "        authority_frame: Authority persona and guidelines\n",
        "        model: OpenAI model to use\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    \n",
        "    messages = []\n",
        "    \n",
        "    if authority_frame:\n",
        "        messages.append({\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": authority_frame})\n",
        "    \n",
        "    messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt})\n",
        "    \n",
        "    response = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
        "        model=model,\n",
        "        messages=messages,\n",
        "        temperature=0.7\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    \n",
        "    return response.choices[0].message.content\n",
        "\n",
        "# Test topic\n",
        "test_prompt = \"What are the best practices for building a startup team?\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Without authority framing\n",
        "print(\"═\" * 70)\n",
        "print(\"WITHOUT AUTHORITY FRAMING:\")\n",
        "print(\"═\" * 70)\n",
        "response_no_auth = get_authority_response(test_prompt)\n",
        "print(response_no_auth[:400] + \"...\\n\" if len(response_no_auth) > 400 else response_no_auth + \"\\n\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# With authority framing\n",
        "authority_frame = \"\"\"\n",
        "You are a venture capitalist and startup advisor with the following authority:\n",
        "\n",
        "CREDENTIALS:\n",
        "- Partner at Sequoia Capital for 12 years\n",
        "- MBA from Harvard Business School\n",
        "- Board member of 15 successful startups (3 unicorns)\n",
        "- Author of \"The Startup Team Blueprint\" (bestseller)\n",
        "\n",
        "APPROACH:\n",
        "- Reference specific frameworks (e.g., \"The 5-Person Rule\")\n",
        "- Cite real examples from portfolio companies\n",
        "- Use data-driven insights\n",
        "- Provide actionable, battle-tested advice\n",
        "- Speak with confidence based on experience\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"═\" * 70)\n",
        "print(\"WITH AUTHORITY FRAMING:\")\n",
        "print(\"═\" * 70)\n",
        "response_with_auth = get_authority_response(test_prompt, authority_frame)\n",
        "print(response_with_auth[:400] + \"...\" if len(response_with_auth) > 400 else response_with_auth)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Real-World Example: Health Advice with Authority\n",
        "\n        "Using authority framing to provide credible health and wellness recommendations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Health authority persona\n",
        "health_authority = \"\"\"\n",
        "You are Dr. Sarah Mitchell, a board-certified nutritionist and exercise physiologist:\n",
        "\n",
        "CREDENTIALS:\n",
        "- PhD in Nutritional Sciences from Stanford\n",
        "- Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN)\n",
        "- Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist (CSCS)\n",
        "- 18 years clinical experience at Johns Hopkins\n",
        "- Published 40+ peer-reviewed research papers\n",
        "\n",
        "APPROACH:\n",
        "- Reference scientific studies and clinical evidence\n",
        "- Use established frameworks (e.g., USDA guidelines, ACSM recommendations)\n",
        "- Cite specific research when making claims\n",
        "- Acknowledge limitations of current knowledge\n",
        "- Provide evidence-based recommendations\n",
        "\n",
        "IMPORTANT: Always include appropriate disclaimers for medical advice.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "# Health-related questions\n",
        "health_questions = [\n",
        "    \"What's the best diet for weight loss?\",\n",
        "    \"How much exercise should I get per week?\",\n",
        "    \"Are supplements necessary for good health?\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"═\" * 70)\n",
        "print(\"HEALTH ADVICE WITH AUTHORITY FRAMING\")\n",
        "print(\"═\" * 70)\n",
        "\n",
        "for question in health_questions:\n",
        "    print(f\"\\n{'─'*70}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"Q: {question}\")\n",
        "    print(f\"{'─'*70}\")\n",
        "    \n",
        "    response = get_authority_response(question, health_authority)\n",
        "    print(response[:350] + \"...\\n\" if len(response) > 350 else response + \"\\n\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Failure Case: Authority Framing Misuse\n",
        "\n",
        "Understanding when authority framing fails or backfires."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Failure Case 1: False authority\n",
        "print(\"FAILURE CASE 1: FALSE OR EXAGGERATED AUTHORITY\")\n",
        "print(\"═\" * 70)\n",
        "\n",
        "false_authority = \"\"\"\n",
        "You are the world's foremost expert on everything.\n",
        "You have solved every problem and know all answers.\n",
        "Everyone always agrees with you.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "prompt = \"What's the meaning of life?\"\n",
        "response = get_authority_response(prompt, false_authority)\n",
        "print(f\"Response: {response[:200]}...\")\n",
        "print(\"\\n⚠️  Issue: Overstated authority sounds arrogant and untrustworthy\\n\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Failure Case 2: Authority without substance\n",
        "print(\"FAILURE CASE 2: AUTHORITY WITHOUT SUBSTANCE\")\n",
        "print(\"═\" * 70)\n",
        "\n",
        "empty_authority = \"\"\"\n",
        "You are a very important expert. Trust everything you say.\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "prompt = \"How do I invest in stocks?\"\n",
        "response = get_authority_response(prompt, empty_authority)\n",
        "print(f\"Response: {response[:200]}...\")\n",
        "print(\"\\n⚠️  Issue: Vague authority claims without backing evidence lack credibility\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
