        "## Tips & Tricks\n",
        "\n",
        "### Building Credible Authority:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Be Specific**: \"Harvard MBA with 10 years at McKinsey\" > \"Business expert\"\n",
        "2. **Use Verifiable Claims**: Credentials that could be checked\n",
        "3. **Reference Frameworks**: Established methodologies add credibility\n",
        "4. **Include Data**: Statistics and research strengthen authority\n",
        "5. **Show Balance**: Acknowledge limitations and alternative views\n",
        "\n",
        "### Authority Frame Template:\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "CREDENTIALS:\n",
        "- [Specific degree/certification]\n",
        "- [Years of relevant experience]\n",
        "- [Notable achievements/positions]\n",
        "- [Publications or recognition]\n",
        "\n",
        "APPROACH:\n",
        "- Reference [specific frameworks/methodologies]\n",
        "- Use [data/research/case studies] to support claims\n",
        "- Provide [evidence-based/actionable] recommendations\n",
        "- Acknowledge [limitations/alternative perspectives]\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "### Model-Specific Notes:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Model | Authority Framing Quality | Notes |\n",
        "|-------|--------------------------|-------|\n",
        "| GPT-4o | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Excellent at maintaining authoritative tone |\n",
        "| Claude 3.5 | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Strong at evidence-based reasoning |\n",
        "| GPT-4o-mini | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Good, benefits from specific frameworks |\n",
        "| Gemini Pro | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ | Capable with clear authority definitions |\n",
        "\n",
        "### Ethical Considerations:\n",
        "- ✅ Use authority to inform and educate\n",
        "- ✅ Include appropriate disclaimers\n",
        "- ✅ Acknowledge uncertainty\n",
        "- ❌ Don't fabricate credentials\n",
        "- ❌ Don't make absolute claims where nuance is needed"
      ]
